{
  "note": "Re-judged 2026-10-24 (independent auditor, authored none of 9c3697d0d1 or 439a413ffd). RFC 8654 Section 3: \"Peers that wish to use the BGP Extended Message Capability MUST support error handling for BGP UPDATE messages per [RFC7606].\" 439a413ffd added a well-formed subtest to TestRFC8654ExtendedMessageSessionUsesRFC7606ErrorHandling and moved the positive tag onto it: on a session negotiating Extended Message both ways, a >4096-octet UPDATE (1100 /24s, valid ORIGIN, AS_PATH, NEXT_HOP) leaves ReadAndProcess error-free, the session Established, exactly one dispatch whose withdrawn section is empty, attribute section byte-equal and NLRI byte-equal to what was sent, and no NOTIFICATION. That is a genuinely conforming input, which closes the previous finding (positive tag on an error input). The negative now names both error subtests: malformed ORIGIN (length 2) dispatches every route as withdrawn with no attributes, session up, no NOTIFICATION; attribute section overrunning the message gives an error, Idle, nothing dispatched and NOTIFICATION 3/1 with empty data. Positive and negative are distinct subtests with distinct inputs. Other carriers unchanged. Discrimination records observed red: positive under session_read.go extendedMessage forced false, negative under the treat-as-withdraw branch forced to None. Units ran green at HEAD.",
